    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "1f6fe1f32e7c44f392f63292e48c2732",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "500e8f11fe5b4883a35fe2bde5fc0b02"
      },
      "name": "AD-07 - Refill Reminders",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-16 (Create Refill Reminder) and UC-17 (Manage Recurring Refill Reminder).\nShows the workflow followed when a Patient or Caregiver creates a medicine refill reminder and optionally configures recurring reminder behaviour.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The user can access the Create Refill Reminder function.\n2. Authentication is treated as a precondition, not part of this workflow, if reminders are restricted to authenticated accounts.\n3. Relevant medicine information is available for selection.\n\nPostconditions (success, no recurrence): A refill reminder is stored with the selected medicine and reminder date/time, scheduled, and confirmed to the user.\nPostconditions (success, with recurrence): The reminder is additionally configured with a validated recurrence pattern; future occurrences are scheduled; confirmation is displayed.\nPostconditions (alternative): Invalid reminder information or invalid recurrence information is rejected and the user is asked to correct it.\n\nScope boundary: A refill reminder is a convenience feature and must not be represented as clinical advice, diagnosis, prescribing, dosage guidance, or treatment recommendation. Recurring behaviour is optional (Should Have) functionality and is not forced on every reminder. No database, API, notification provider, or backend is modeled as an actor. No purchasing, ordering, payment, or delivery functionality is included.\n\nModeling note: 'Request Correction' following the reminder-information validation loops back to 'Select / Enter Medicine', the first step of the local input sequence, so the user can re-enter medicine and/or date/time together; 'Request Correction' following the recurrence validation loops back to 'Select Recurrence Pattern' as explicitly specified.\n\nTraceability: UC-16 - Create Refill Reminder (FR-32-FR-34); UC-17 - Manage Recurring Refill Reminder (FR-32-FR-34; optional/Should Have).",
      "ownedElements": [
